course: dictionary
lesson: 9745
title: Superb: a strong word of praise
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: «Superb» is a strong word of praise. It means extremely good, or excellent. When a writer says «a superb hunter», they are saying the owl is far better at hunting than most animals, not just a little better.
explain: Superb is stronger than «good» and «great». If you read «The meal was good», the meal was fine. If you read «The meal was superb», the meal was brilliant. Look at the words around it to check: «Real rats have a superb sense of smell» tells you the smell is extremely good, not just nice.
explain: Superb can also mean very grand and beautiful to look at, like «a superb view». Teachers write «Superb work!» on pages, and sports commentators say «a superb goal». Try swapping in «extremely good» to see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Superb means extremely good, or excellent.
fact: Superb can also mean very grand and beautiful to look at.
fact: «Superb» is a stronger word of praise than «good» or «great».
fact: «Superb» is a little more formal than «awesome», so it suits reports and school work.
fact: Superbly is the adverb form, as in «She played superbly».
exercise: «Real rats have a superb sense of smell and taste.» What does superb mean here? | Very small | Dreadful and smelly | *Extremely good | Hungry
exercise: Teacher writes «Superb work!» on Mia's page. What does the teacher mean? | Her work is late | Her work is too short | Her work is untidy | *Her work is extremely good
exercise: Which word is a strong word of praise, stronger than good? | Damp | *Superb | Sleepy | Ordinary
test: «Owls are expert hunters with superb hearing.» In this sentence, superb means? | Strange and noisy | Very quiet | Broken | *Extremely good
test: Which phrase describes a view that is very grand and beautiful? | A broken chair | A dull grey wall | *A superb view | A tiny crumb
exam: Why might a writer choose superb instead of good? | *It is a stronger word of praise, showing something was far better than ordinary | It is the name of a bird | It means the same as bad | It is only used for food
